# Data files (don't commit API responses)
# Data lifecycle: raw, external, interim and processed trees are regenerated
# by code and never versioned. Provenance records, the two HUD schedules the
# API does not serve, fixtures and schemas are committed.
data/raw/
data/external/
data/interim/
data/processed/
!data/README.md
!data/fixtures/
!data/fixtures/**
!data/schemas/
!data/schemas/**

# Bulk third-party downloads: the BYTES stay out of git, the PIN goes in.
# krl_tutorials_data.connectors.BulkFileSource records the URL, vintage and
# SHA-256, so SOURCES.md reproduces the acquisition without committing ~15 MB
# of a publisher's file into permanent history.
#
# data/hud/ is DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED HERE. Those files are U.S. Government
# works in the public domain, they total under 1 MB, and `huduser.gov` is
# refused by the egress allowlist in the environment these notebooks execute in
# -- so the committed copy is the only way D05 is reproducible at all. The pin
# in data/hud/fmr/SOURCES.md is what reproduces them where the host IS
# reachable. Zillow's terms are not equivalent, hence the rule below.
data/zillow/**/*.csv
data/zillow/**/*.csv.gz
data/zillow/**/*.zip
data/zillow/**/*.xlsx

# Internal planning/metadata (not for public repo)
.github/REPOSITORY_METADATA.md
.github/TOPICS.txt
.github/DESCRIPTION.md
.github/discussions/
docs/wiki/README.md
*_INTERNAL*.md
*_PLANNING*.md
_to_delete/

# --- added during the public-readiness pass, 2026-09-18 ---
# A literal "~" directory, created when a shell quoted the home path wrong.
# It held 15 cache files and 6.2 MB of nothing anyone wanted.
~/

# No archives. Three copies of a 56 MB Google Cloud CLI tarball were tracked in
# notebooks/10_advanced_nlp/D34_media_intelligence/ -- 168 MB of vendor binary,
# 58% of everything the repository tracked, referenced by no file and absent
# from the audit manifest.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# Agent and tooling scratch that appears at the repo root.
Claude outputs/
.forensics/

# NOTE: notebooks_v2/**/provenance/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those records
# are committed evidence. A provenance/ directory at the REPO ROOT is the
# defect, and tests/test_provenance_location.py fails on it.
